<%# The "Mobile background" CTA — on EVERY editor card, whatever its panel
    holds, because every card has a question and answers on a phone and that
    is what this designs: the area behind them, below the header where the
    card has one (shared/_card_component paints it on .split-right).

    One partial rather than a button per media branch of _split_left so the
    four branches cannot drift — the same class (.card-bg-fab, which the
    device frame's dock and the preview's chrome audit both key on), the same
    action (media-picker#openMobileBackground, which aims the picker at
    card.mobile_bg and nothing else) and the same words on every type. It is
    never hidden when media lands, unlike the header backdrop's pill: a
    picture in the header says nothing about what sits below it. %>
<button type="button" class="add-bg-fab card-bg-fab"
        data-action="click->media-picker#openMobileBackground"
        title="<%= t("editor.mobile_background_title", default: "Colour, image or GIF behind this card's question and answers on a phone") %>">
  <span><%= t("editor.mobile_background", default: "Mobile background") %></span>
</button>
